Q: I need the path of the file that is invoking the launch of my Python application A: <p>My example uses PySide6. However, the approach should be identical in PyQt6.</p>
<p>First, subclass <code>QApplication</code> and intercept all events. You only need to handle events of type <code>FileOpen</code>. All other events should be passed to the superclass for processing. This allows you to easily retrieve the path of the file.</p>
<p>If the command-line argument approach is used instead, the file path is available in the first element of the <code>sys.argv</code> list.</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>import sys
from PySide6.QtCore import QEvent
from PySide6.QtGui import QFileOpenEvent
from PySide6.QtWidgets import QApplication, QMainWindow
from typing import cast


class App(QApplication):

    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):
        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)
        self.main_window = None

    def set_main_window(self, window):
        self.main_window = window

    def event(self, event):
        if event.type() == QEvent.Type.FileOpen:
            open_event = cast(QFileOpenEvent, event)
            file_path = open_event.file()

            if self.main_window:
                self.main_window.set_title_text(file_path)

        return super().event(event)

class MainWindow(QMainWindow):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.setWindowTitle('Untitled File')

    def set_title_text(self, text):
        self.setWindowTitle(text)


def main():
    app = App(sys.argv)
    win = MainWindow()
    app.set_main_window(win)
    win.show()

    if len(sys.argv) &gt; 1:
        window.set_title_text(sys.argv[1])

    sys.exit(app.exec())

if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
</code></pre>
<p>To make PyInstaller add the appropriate entries to the application's <code>Info.plist</code> file, you need to edit the <code>main.spec</code> file and add a section to the <code>BUNDLE</code> definition.</p>
